This project uses the Tkinter framework in Python for creating the graphical user interface (GUI).

Key Points about Tkinter in this Project:
Tkinter: Tkinter is the standard GUI library for Python, used to create windows, dialogs, buttons, and other GUI components. It is a wrapper around the Tk GUI toolkit.

Key Components Used:

Tk(): Creates the main window of the application.
Button: A clickable button, used to trigger different actions such as adding, viewing, updating, or deleting contacts.
messagebox: A module from Tkinter used to display informational, warning, or error messages in pop-up windows.
simpledialog: A module from Tkinter that provides simple dialog boxes for getting user input, such as asking for a contact name or phone number.
pack(): A geometry manager in Tkinter used to organize and display widgets (like buttons) inside the window.
configure(bg=...): This sets the background color of the main window.
Why Tkinter?
Simple and Lightweight: Tkinter is easy to use and ideal for small to medium-sized desktop applications.
Cross-platform: Tkinter works on all major platforms (Windows, macOS, Linux) without requiring any additional installation, as it comes bundled with Python.
Quick Development: Tkinter provides a simple way to develop GUI applications without needing to learn more complex frameworks or tools.
Conclusion:
The framework used in this project is Tkinter, which is the built-in GUI toolkit for Python. It allows the creation of interactive desktop applications with components like buttons, input dialogs, and message boxes.







